# Mockito 5 defaults to the inline mock maker, which instruments the full type hierarchy of a mock and
# cannot redefine JDK bootstrap classes. Since Java 19, ExecutorService extends AutoCloseable, so mocking
# ScheduledExecutorService reaches java.lang.AutoCloseable and java.lang.Object and fails; mocking
# java.nio.file.FileSystem fails for the same reason. The subclass mock maker proxies instead of
# retransforming, which is sufficient here: every mocked type is a non-final interface or abstract class.
mock-maker-subclass
